### Roadmap

- [Overview](https://ethereum.org/roadmap/): The future of Ethereum
- [Improved security](https://ethereum.org/roadmap/security/): Ethereum's roadmap hardens block production and censorship resistance today while preparing the protocol for the quantum era and decades of reliable operation.
- [Cheaper transactions](https://ethereum.org/roadmap/scaling/): Rollups batch transactions together offchain, reducing costs for the user. However, the way rollups currently use data is too expensive, limiting how cheap transactions can be. Proto-Danksharding fixes this.
- [Better user experience](https://ethereum.org/roadmap/user-experience/): It is still too complex to use Ethereum for most people. To encourage mass adoption, Ethereum must drastically lower its barriers to entry - users must get the benefits of decentralized, permissionless and censorship resistant access to Ethereum but it must be as frictionless as using a traditional web2 app.
- [Privacy](https://ethereum.org/roadmap/privacy/): Ethereum is working to make privacy a first-class property of the network through upgrades that protect transaction privacy, secure user data access, and enable verifiable but private identity.

